  "interpretation": "protocol_b scores Node-MoE's differentiated ChebNetII pool under the same honest fixed-expert protocol as the repo's 0/234 null: the pool is routing-blind and the gate is cross-fit on disjoint nodes. faithful_joint is the paper's own end-to-end training. uniform_ensemble_vs_global_chebnetii refutes (or confirms) ensemble capacity: an unrouted equal-weight average of the same experts matching a single global ChebNetII means extra expert capacity is not the source. gate_effect_joint_vs_uniform_ensemble is the causal control: the gated model minus the same experts averaged, so a positive value localises the gain to gate-expert co-adaptation -- which collapses under protocol_b's cross-fit gate. A win in faithful_joint but not protocol_b therefore means the gain is not a routing signal that survives honest evaluation."
